  description: A galaxy is a vast system of stars, planetary systems, gas, dust,
    and dark matter held together by gravity. Galaxies come in different shapes,
    including spiral, elliptical, and irregular forms, and can contain millions or
    billions of stars.
  interestingFact: Galaxies can collide and merge over billions of years, changing
    their shapes and influencing how new stars form.
